==History==
2020
*The Skeleton Dragons were once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Skeleton Dragons Draft Challenge]], which started on 5/6/2020. In this challenge, gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Skeleton Dragons. If the player achieved at least 3 wins, they obtained the Skeleton Dragons early.
*The Skeleton Dragons card was generally released on 6/7/2020, in the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (6/7/2020)|July 2020 Update]].
*On 7/7/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/7/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Skeleton Dragons' damage by 6%.
*On 31/8/2020, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20II%20Update%20(31/8/2020)|Clan Wars II Update]], changed the Skeleton Dragons' sound effects. Previously, their sound effects were identical to those of the [[Minions]].
*On 6/10/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Skeleton Dragons' attack time interval to 1.9 seconds (from 1.7 seconds).
2021
*On 30/3/2021, the [[Version History#2021%20Quarter%201%20Update%20(30/3/2021)|2021 Quarter 1 Update]], added the Skeleton Dragons to all Draft selections.
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Skeleton Dragons from Spooky Town to P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 30/3/2022, the [[Version History#Miner%20Update%20(30/3/2022)|Miner Update]], fixed an issue where the Skeleton Dragons' [[Star Points|Star Level]] used the sound effects of the [[Baby Dragon]].
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Skeleton Dragons from P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse to Spell Valley.
2023
*On 6/6/2023, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(6/6/2023)|Balance Update]], increased the Skeleton Dragons' hitpoints by 5.8%. It also increased the distance between the Skeleton Dragons upon deployment.
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 6/8/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2024)|Balance Update]], decreased the Skeleton Dragons' hitpoints by 0.5%.

